course: dictionary
lesson: 9112
title: Smelly and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Smelly means having a bad, strong smell. You can find its meaning in the words around it. «A skunk can spray a very smelly liquid» tells you the liquid is strong and unpleasant, and the skunk's spray is a warning.
explain: Smelly can also be used to tease people. «Kieran calls Lily «Smelly Lily» in front of the class.» The name is not about a real smell. Kieran says it to be unkind, so the context shows the word is hurtful here.
explain: Smelly is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «smelly socks» or a smelly bin. Its other forms are smellier and smelliest. Use context and a dictionary together to check a word's meaning.
fact: Smelly means having a bad, strong smell.
fact: Smelly is an adjective, and its forms are smellier and smelliest.
fact: Smelly things include old socks, bins and fish left out.
fact: A smell can warn us of danger, like food that has gone bad.
fact: Washing, clean clothes and deodorant help us stop being smelly.
exercise: What does smelly mean in «a very smelly liquid» from the skunk sentence? | Sticky and sweet | *Having a bad, strong smell | Very loud and noisy | Bright and shiny
exercise: Kieran calls Lily «Smelly Lily» in front of the class. What does this tell you about the nickname? | It is a name for a famous singer | It is a kind name for a friend | *It is a teasing, unkind name | It is the name of a flower
exercise: Find and copy the word that means having a bad smell in «the arm looks thin, hairy and smelly». | *smelly | thin | hairy | arm
test: A ladybird bleeds a bitter, smelly yellow liquid when it is attacked. What does smelly tell you about the liquid? | It is sweet and tasty | *It has a strong, bad smell | It is clear like water | It has no smell at all
test: Chòu means smelly in Chinese, and it appears in «chòuměi». What does chòuměi mean? | Sad and tired | Very hungry | *Vain, too pleased with yourself about looks | Clean and fresh
exam: Which sentence uses smelly to mean having a bad, strong smell? | The sun was smelly and bright over the hill. | The smelly song made everyone cheer and dance. | Kieran is a smelly name for a singer. | *The bin behind the shop was smelly and full of rotten fish.
